    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      282.17,
      401.86,
      305.51
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Mines and Minerals(Amendment) Act, No. of 2013.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      314.09,
      401.91,
      361.43
    ],
    "text": "2.Section 28 of the Mines and Minerals Act, No. 33 of1992 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) ishereby amended by the addition of a new subsectionimmediately after subsection (4) as follows :\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      173.85,
      370.13,
      401.9,
      429.47
    ],
    "text": "\u201c(5) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in anyother provisions of this Act, the Minister may, from timeto time, with the written recommendation of the Bureau,prescribe such minerals required for construction purposeswhich requires a licence for transportation of the same.\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      438.17,
      401.9,
      497.51
    ],
    "text": "3.Section 33 of the principal enactment is herebyamended in subsection (1) of that section, by the substitutionfor the words \u201cradioactive elements and coral\u201d of the words\u201cradioactive elements, ilmenite, rutile, zircon, garnet,monazite, coral\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      506.09,
      401.9,
      529.43
    ],
